{"data":{"repository":{"issueOrPullRequest":{"__typename":"PullRequest","number":14927,"updatedAt":"2026-11-13T12:06:21Z","createdAt":"2026-11-03T21:20:00Z","lastEditedAt":"2026-11-03T21:29:03Z","body":"> [Prototype overview and documentation](https://cli.github.io/multi-account-docs/)\n>\n> **DO NOT MERGE.** This stack is almost entirely vibe coded. These drafts are for handy review and prototyping, not merging as-is.\n>\n> Expect the code to be really bad in places: highly coupled, handling edge cases that do not really matter, or doing suspiciously fragile things like parsing GraphQL request bodies.\n>\n> I suspect some of the suspicious code also exposes the complexity of this feature set, because account selection, Git configuration, scope precedence, worktrees, SSH and API requests all interact.\n>\n> The prototype experience is the purpose, not the code. I want to find out whether the experience is useful, not defend this implementation or treat it as a design to preserve.\n\n<!--\nThank you for contributing to GitHub CLI!\n\nIf you are proposing a fix for a security issue, STOP and follow .github/SECURITY.md instead.\n\nKeep the entire pull request self-contained, reviewer-facing, and diegetic: describe the\nchange, rationale, and evidence within the context of the repository and pull request. Do not\nnarrate how the pull request was produced or refer to private conversations, prior agent work,\nor other behind-the-scenes context. Omit those details unless they materially affect review;\nif they do, state the relevant fact and its significance directly.\n-->\n\n<!-- List related issues here. Use `fixes` or `closes` keywords to associate an issue number. -->\n\n### Description\n\n<!--\nWhat's the problem? How are we addressing it?\n\nWrite for a reviewer who has not worked in this part of the codebase. Give them the\nbackground they need before the problem makes sense, and avoid jargon.\n-->\n\nFollow on from https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14926\n\nEvaluating persistent authentication changes needs a clear setup path and a way to isolate the experiment. This PR adds guided setup, developer evaluation tools and debug-only keyring isolation.\n\nLayer 8 of an eight-part prototype review stack. This is a way to review the design and implementation in smaller pieces, not a proposal to merge the current stack as-is.\n\n### How did you test this change?\n\n<!--\nReport only actions you actually performed and results you actually observed, using factual\nfirst-person language (for example, \"I ran...\" and \"I saw...\"). Do not present planned,\nhypothetical, inferred, or merely expected scenarios as testing.\n\nAutomated test results do not belong here. Passing unit tests, `go test ./...` output, and\ncoverage numbers tell a reviewer nothing they cannot see from CI, so do not paste them.\n\nIf you did not exercise the changed behavior, write `Not tested` and explain why.\n\nUse one or more of these, whichever communicates best:\n\n1. Screenshots or GIFs of the real command running. Preferred whenever the change is visible\n   in terminal output. If output changed, show it before and after.\n2. Given/When/Then scenarios, but only when you actually executed the steps. For example:\n   Given I was in a repo with no open pull requests\n   When I ran `gh pr list`\n   Then I saw \"no open pull requests in cli/cli\"\n3. A natural language walkthrough of what you did by hand, the states you covered, and what\n   you saw, including error and edge cases.\n\nIf you leave this empty, your pull request will very likely be closed.\n-->\n\nI exercised the debug keyring-isolation capability and reset in disposable configuration. I read the actual global and managed files before reset, then saw the user include remain and authenticated with the retained real account.\n\n```text\n$ cat ~/.gitconfig; cat ~/.ordinary.gitconfig\n[include]\n\tpath = /Users/Shared/gc-H8vKqb/r-5aVX8u/home/.ordinary.gitconfig\n[user]\n\tname = Ordinary Author\n\temail = ordinary@example.invalid\n```\n\n#### Reset privately before returning to stable gh\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bd457de9-43eb-49ef-aba9-c7ca5d4b1592\n\n#### Verify the debug runner prerequisite before using accounts\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/67d5d26d-de84-45a5-8778-bacda9a569c3\n\n### Key points\n\n<!--\nTradeoffs you accepted, alternatives you rejected, and anything a reviewer would otherwise have to guess at.\n-->\n\nThis layer adds evaluation and setup tooling, not a new identity storage format. The reset recording exercises cleanup already available in the stack so reviewers can see how to return to ordinary configuration.\n\nLive evaluation tools are optional and can create GitHub resources. The offline review scripts use synthetic accounts and deny network and Keychain access. Real-account recordings are separate from those scripts.\n\n### Notes for reviewers\n\n<!--\nWhere should review start, and what should be read next? Call out anything you are unsure about.\n\nLink related issues or prior discussion, with one sentence on why each matters.\n-->\n\nStart with the setup approval boundaries, then isolation and cleanup. The guided-agent workflow and full live acceptance runner were not exercised for these recordings. Reset managed configuration before removing a prerelease executable referenced by Git.\n\nThe recordings use the product code at this layer, not a later stack endpoint. The included offline replay scripts are supplementary and do not reproduce the live-account recordings.\n\n<details><summary>Offline replay on macOS</summary>\n\nBuild this layer, then run its synthetic scenario with an absolute executable path. This is a replay instruction, not a claim that the command below was used to make the videos.\n\n```sh\nmake\nenv -i HOME=\"$HOME\" PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin \\\n  /bin/bash script/multiaccount-review/08-reset.sh --gh \"$PWD/bin/gh\" --stable-gh /absolute/path/to/stable/gh\n```\n\n</details>\n\n### Authorship and follow-up\n\n<!--\nREQUIRED - If you are an AI agent filling in this template, answer \"Who wrote this\" for yourself and answer honestly. For \"Who answers review comments,\" use only a choice the human has explicitly made in the conversation. If no choice has already been established, pause and ask the human to choose one of the three options before creating or updating the pull request. Do not infer the choice from repository ownership, authorship, assignees, prior interactions, or the current operator. After the human answers, check exactly the option they chose; the last option is valid when the human explicitly chooses nobody.\n\nCheck exactly one box in each list.\n-->\n\nWho wrote this:\n\n- [ ] A human wrote it.\n- [x] An agent wrote it under close human direction.\n- [ ] An agent wrote it independently, and no human has guided the implementation beyond the initial prompt.\n\nWho answers review comments:\n\n- [ ] @username will read and reply directly. Name the account.\n- [ ] An agent will draft replies and @username will read them before they are posted.\n- [x] Nobody has explicitly committed to replying.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nPrototype behaviour under review:\n\n**Given** a developer explicitly chooses to evaluate the prototype.\n\n**When** the isolated workflow is used and the experiment is reset.\n\n**Then** managed identity wiring is removed while ordinary user configuration and saved accounts remain.\n\n**DO NOT MERGE**\n","author":{"__typename":"User","login":"williammartin"},"comments":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]},"reviews":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"author":{"__typename":"Bot","login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"state":"COMMENTED","submittedAt":"2026-11-03T21:27:59Z","lastEditedAt":null,"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nOffline fixtures still access the operator’s native keyring, while other active findings identify broken standard acceptance runs, lost API gateway routing, and